{"actor":"EO:12379","date":"1982-08-17","mechanism":"revocation","source":{"page_or_item":"42 U.S.C. 3001 note; note 'Executive Order No. 11022' [USLM note id id3aa453c2-c3e9-11f1-bd73-d95596aaa024]; usc42.xml (sha256 9a2ce8ea01dfa97423fcd8749e7534a64c0ec75df9bf56584b210c0725a66692) in xml_uscAll@119-121.zip","sha256":"c6122974e951003437ece5a998aa7c0b2cdc0f5703dfc78d6135e1fc9e729142","url":"https://uscode.house.gov/download/releasepoints/us/pl/119/121/xml_uscAll@119-121.zip"}},"suggested":true}],"whole_order_end_total":1},"provisional_status":"no","readiness":{"by_step":{"clause_inventory":"confirm","counterevidence":"resolve_conflicts","ending_or_current_basis":"confirm","opus_media":"n/a","original_text":"confirm","savings_residuals":"agent_judgment","shared_sources":"n/a"},"needs_research":[],"would_satisfy_once_confirmed":["original_text","clause_inventory","ending_or_current_basis"]},"shared_sources":[],"signing_dates_seen":{"fr-originals@jobs/fr-originals/output":"1962-05-14","later-events_catalog":"1962-05-14","stage19_causal_queue":"1962-05-14"},"source_ladder_exhausted_proposed":[],"status":"MACHINE DRAFT - UNVERIFIED; not a claim; see jobs/claim-drafts/AGENT_GUIDE.md"},"claim":{"instrument_id":"EO:11022","later_source_search":[],"operative_clauses":[{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(a) There is hereby established the President’s Council \non Aging (hereinafter referred to as the “ Council” ) .","original_source":{"page_or_item":"27 FR 4659, PDF pages 5-5; Sec. 1(a)","sha256":"56b46770ca89bc4f1e85cec8842eb0e28a4dd0cfb466a6513647bdeeb7dceba2","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1962-05-17/pdf/FR-1962-05-17.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:11022#sec1(a)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(b) The Council shall be composed of the Secretary of Health, \nEducation, and Welfare, who shall be Chairman, the Secretary of \nAgriculture, the Secretary of Commerce, the Secretary of Labor, the \nSecretary of the Treasury, the Chairman of the Civil Service Commis­\nsion, the Administrator of the Housing and Home Finance Agency, \nand the Administrator of Veterans’ Affairs.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"27 FR 4659, PDF pages 5-5; Sec. 1(b)","sha256":"56b46770ca89bc4f1e85cec8842eb0e28a4dd0cfb466a6513647bdeeb7dceba2","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1962-05-17/pdf/FR-1962-05-17.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:11022#sec1(b)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(c) The Chairman of the Council shall invite the head of any other \nFederal department or agency to attend any meeting of the Council \nat which any matter within or affecting the area o f responsibility of \nsuch department or agency is considered and to be a temporary member \nwith respect to such matter.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"27 FR 4659, PDF pages 5-5; Sec. 1(c)","sha256":"56b46770ca89bc4f1e85cec8842eb0e28a4dd0cfb466a6513647bdeeb7dceba2","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1962-05-17/pdf/FR-1962-05-17.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:11022#sec1(c)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"S ec. 2. The Council shall:","original_source":{"page_or_item":"27 FR 4659, PDF pages 5-5; Sec. 2 (lead-in)","sha256":"56b46770ca89bc4f1e85cec8842eb0e28a4dd0cfb466a6513647bdeeb7dceba2","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1962-05-17/pdf/FR-1962-05-17.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:11022#sec2","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(a) Maintain a continuing study of the overall responsibilities of \nthe Federal Government with respect to the problems of the aging and \nmake recommendations to the President concerning policies and pro­\ngrams required to meet Federal responsibilities, particularly on mat­\nters which do not fall within the jurisdiction o f a single agency.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"27 FR 4659, PDF pages 5-5; Sec. 2(a)","sha256":"56b46770ca89bc4f1e85cec8842eb0e28a4dd0cfb466a6513647bdeeb7dceba2","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1962-05-17/pdf/FR-1962-05-17.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:11022#sec2(a)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(b) Identify matters which require coordinated action by two or \nmore Federal agencies and make appropriate arrangements for joint \nor coordinated action, including, as appropriate, conferences, ^oint \nstudies, and the development o f recommendations to the President.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"27 FR 4659, PDF pages 5-5; Sec. 2(b)","sha256":"56b46770ca89bc4f1e85cec8842eb0e28a4dd0cfb466a6513647bdeeb7dceba2","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1962-05-17/pdf/FR-1962-05-17.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:11022#sec2(b)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(c) Promote the sharing and dissemination of information on the \nneeds of the aging and policies and programs relating to the aging, \namong Federal departments and agencies and between them and \nState, local, or private agencies and organizations having functions \nor interests in fields relating to the problems o f the aging.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"27 FR 4659, PDF pages 5-5; Sec. 2(c)","sha256":"56b46770ca89bc4f1e85cec8842eb0e28a4dd0cfb466a6513647bdeeb7dceba2","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1962-05-17/pdf/FR-1962-05-17.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:11022#sec2(c)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(d) Prepare an annual consolidated report to the President con­\ncerning the activities of the Council and the several Federal depart­\nments and agencies having programs relating to the aging.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"27 FR 4659, PDF pages 5-5; Sec. 2(d)","sha256":"56b46770ca89bc4f1e85cec8842eb0e28a4dd0cfb466a6513647bdeeb7dceba2","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1962-05-17/pdf/FR-1962-05-17.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:11022#sec2(d)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(a) Consonant with law, each department or agency repre­\nsented on the Council shall, as may be necessary for the effectuation \no f the purpose of this order, furnish assistance to the Council in \naccordance with Section 214 o f the Act of May 3, 1945, 59 Stat. 134 \n(31 U.S.C. 691).","original_source":{"page_or_item":"27 FR 4659, PDF pages 5-5; Sec. 3(a)","sha256":"56b46770ca89bc4f1e85cec8842eb0e28a4dd0cfb466a6513647bdeeb7dceba2","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1962-05-17/pdf/FR-1962-05-17.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:11022#sec3(a)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(b) Other Federal departments and agencies are also authorized \nand directed, to the extent not inconsistent with law, to cooperate \nwith the Council and to furnish it such information and assistance \nas it may find necessary in the performance o f its functions.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"27 FR 4659, PDF pages 5-5; Sec. 3(b)","sha256":"56b46770ca89bc4f1e85cec8842eb0e28a4dd0cfb466a6513647bdeeb7dceba2","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1962-05-17/pdf/FR-1962-05-17.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:11022#sec3(b)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"S ec. 4. The Federal Council on Aging, established by a letter from \nthe President to the Secretary of Health, Education, and Welfare, \ndated March 7, 1959, is hereby abolished and that letter is hereby \nsuperseded.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"27 FR 4659, PDF pages 5-5; Sec. 4","sha256":"56b46770ca89bc4f1e85cec8842eb0e28a4dd0cfb466a6513647bdeeb7dceba2","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1962-05-17/pdf/FR-1962-05-17.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:11022#sec4","state_at_cutoff":null}],"original_representation":{"page_or_item":"27 FR 4659, PDF pages 5-5","sha256":"56b46770ca89bc4f1e85cec8842eb0e28a4dd0cfb466a6513647bdeeb7dceba2","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1962-05-17/pdf/FR-1962-05-17.pdf"},"research_rationale":"","savings_residuals":null,"schema":"eo-lifecycle-claim/v1","unresolved_material_gaps":["DRAFT: state_at_cutoff not decided for 11 clause(s); clause inventory completeness not confirmed","DRAFT: whole-order ending not established","DRAFT: savings and residual effects not closed","DRAFT: later_source_search not recorded (machine searches are proposals only; paste them after judging them adequate and resolving every CONFLICT line)","CONFLICT FULL_AND_PARTIAL_EVIDENCE_CONFLICT: EO:12379: the sources read as both a whole and a partial ending"],"whole_order_end":null,"whole_order_status":"no"},"draft_schema":"eo-claim-draft/v1","instrument_id":"EO:11022"}
